---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/PageHero.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { GA_MEASUREMENT_ID, POLICY_LAST_UPDATED, SITE } from '@/lib/site';

// The host is known at build time: Vercel builds set VERCEL; other builds are for Hostinger.
const HOST = process.env.VERCEL ? 'Vercel' : 'Hostinger';
const MAIL = process.env.VERCEL ? 'an email delivery provider' : "the host's email service";
const updated = new Date(`${POLICY_LAST_UPDATED}T00:00:00Z`).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' });
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How NeoKemetAI handles information: what is collected when you visit, advertising and analytics cookies, contact-form messages, YouTube embeds and third-party links."
>
  <PageHero kicker="Privacy" title="Privacy policy" glyph="𓂀">
    <Breadcrumbs slot="above" items={[{ label: 'Privacy', href: '/privacy/' }]} />
  </PageHero>

  <div class="container section prose policy">
    <div class="updated">Last updated: <time datetime={POLICY_LAST_UPDATED}>{updated}</time></div>

    <p>
      {SITE.name} is an educational website about ancient Egypt. We aim to collect as little information about visitors as
      possible. This policy explains what information is involved when you use the site, and why.
    </p>

    <h2>Visiting the site</h2>
    <p>
      You can read every page without creating an account or giving us any personal information. The site is served as
      static pages by our hosting provider, {HOST}. Like any web server, its infrastructure receives technical information
      needed to deliver pages and protect the service, such as your IP address, browser type, the page requested and the time
      of the request. This information is handled by {HOST} under its own privacy policy and is kept in short-lived server
      logs; we do not use it to identify visitors.
    </p>

    <h2 id="analytics">Analytics</h2>
    {GA_MEASUREMENT_ID ? (
      <>
        <p>
          With your permission, we use Google Analytics 4 (Google LLC) to understand how the site is used: which pages are
          visited, roughly where visitors come from (country or city level), the device and browser type, and how people
          arrive (for example from a search engine or social media). We use this only to improve the site; we do not use it
          to identify you, and analytics data is not used to target advertising.
        </p>
        <p>
          Google Analytics is not loaded until you choose "Allow" in the banner shown on your first visit. If you choose
          "Decline", or make no choice, nothing is sent to Google Analytics. You can change your choice at any time with
          "Cookie settings" at the bottom of every page. Google processes this information under
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a>;
          analytics data is kept for the retention period set in our Google Analytics account (14 months at most).
        </p>
      </>
    ) : (
      <p>
        The site does not currently use any analytics, advertising or tracking service. If we add analytics in the future, we
        will update this policy before doing so.
      </p>
    )}

    <h2 id="advertising">Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is free to use, and we use Google AdSense (Google LLC) to show advertisements on some pages to help cover
      the cost of running the site. Advertising never changes what we write: our pages are not sponsored, and we do not choose
      the individual ads you see.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to this website or
        other websites.
      </li>
      <li>
        Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to our visitors based on their visits to
        this site and/or other sites on the Internet.
      </li>
      <li>
        You may opt out of personalised advertising by visiting Google's
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ads Settings</a>. You can also opt
        out of some other third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalised advertising at
        <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.aboutads.info</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you do not opt out, or have not given consent where it is required, you may still see ads that are not
      personalised, based on the page you are reading and your general location. Visitors in the European Economic Area, the
      United Kingdom and Switzerland are asked for their consent through a consent message before advertising cookies are
      used for personalised ads, and can change that choice at any time. More detail on how Google uses information from
      sites that use its services is at
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    {GA_MEASUREMENT_ID ? (
      <p>
        {SITE.name} itself sets no cookies. If you allow analytics, Google Analytics sets its own cookies (named
        <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>) to recognise repeat visits. Your analytics choice is remembered in your
        browser's local storage (<code>nk-consent</code>), not in a cookie. Where advertising is shown, Google and its partners
        may set advertising cookies as described under <a href="#advertising">Advertising</a>. Fonts are served from our own site, not from a
        third-party font service. Other third-party services described below may set their own cookies only when you choose to
        use them.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p>
        {SITE.name} does not set cookies and does not use local storage to track you. Fonts are served from our own site, not
        from a third-party font service. Third-party services described below may set their own cookies only when you choose to
        use them.
      </p>
    )}

    <h2>YouTube videos</h2>
    <p>
      Pages that feature a NeoKemet film show a preview image loaded from YouTube's image servers (<code>i.ytimg.com</code>),
      which means YouTube receives the standard technical information of that image request. The video player itself is not
      loaded until you click play. It then loads from <code>youtube-nocookie.com</code>, YouTube's privacy-enhanced mode, and
      from that point YouTube (Google) may collect information and set cookies under
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Interactive 3D models, maps and games</h2>
    <p>
      3D models, the Valley of the Kings map and their viewers are loaded from this site only, and no third-party service is
      involved. The game Rise of Waset and the Pyramid Builder Lab keep your progress and settings in your own browser's local
      storage so you can continue later; this information never leaves your device, and you can remove it by clearing your
      browser's site data.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact form</h2>
    <p>
      When you use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>, we receive the name, email address, subject and message you
      enter. The form is processed on our hosting provider ({HOST}) and delivered to our inbox through {MAIL}. We use this information only to read and reply to your message; we do not add you to a mailing list,
      sell it or share it for marketing. The form includes simple automatic spam checks that do not involve any third-party
      tracking.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep information</h2>
    <p>
      Contact messages are kept in our email for as long as needed to deal with your enquiry and for a reasonable period
      afterwards for reference, then deleted. You can ask us to delete your message at any time. Server logs are kept by our
      hosting provider for a limited period according to its own policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to other websites and social media</h2>
    <p>
      Our pages link to museums, archives, academic publications and reference works, and our footer links to NeoKemetAI
      profiles on YouTube, Facebook, X (Twitter), TikTok, Instagram and Pinterest. Those links open the other site, which has its own
      privacy practices; we are not responsible for them. Following a social media link does not share any information from
      {SITE.name} with that platform beyond what your browser normally sends when opening a page.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>The services involved in running the site are:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>{HOST}</strong>: hosting, the contact form and our email.</li>
      {HOST === 'Vercel' && <li><strong>An email delivery provider</strong>: forwarding contact-form messages to our inbox.</li>}
      <li><strong>YouTube (Google)</strong>: video preview images, and the player once you press play.</li>
      {GA_MEASUREMENT_ID && <li><strong>Google Analytics (Google)</strong>: visitor statistics, only if you allow them.</li>}
      <li><strong>Google AdSense (Google)</strong>: advertising, as described above.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Each processes information under its own privacy policy.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is suitable for learners of all ages but does not knowingly collect personal information from children.
      Children should ask a parent, guardian or teacher before sending us a message.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have the right to ask what personal information we hold about you, to correct it
      or to have it deleted. Because we hold very little, the only personal information we are likely to have is a message
      you sent us. Contact us and we will help.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy when the site changes, for example if we add a new service. The date at the top of the page
      shows when it was last revised.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>For any privacy question or request, please use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .updated { color: var(--text-faint); font-size: var(--step--1); margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
  .policy h2 { margin-top: 2.2rem; }
</style>
